  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At the foot of the Rayol village, this pebble-and-sand beach enjoys a green setting, right below the famous Domaine du Rayol and its terraced Mediterranean garden. Open views across the bay, between Cavalaire and Le Lavandou.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Dogs are allowed on this beach, but banned from 8am to 7pm between 1 June and 30 September, a seasonal rule confirmed both by the Golfe de Saint-Tropez tourist office and by the town hall itself in its municipal newsletter "Carnets du Rayol-Canadel-Pramousquier" — the same rule as on the neighbouring <a href="/en/fiche-canadel">Canadel</a> and <a href="/en/fiche-plage-pramousquier-rayol-canadel">Pramousquier</a> beaches. Outside that period or those hours, access is free, provided you pick up after your dog.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come early morning or late in the day in high summer to enjoy the beach with your dog, or visit in autumn or spring for free access all day.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Domaine du Rayol, a remarkable garden overlooking the beach, does not allow dogs, even on leash — worth knowing if you're planning to visit both. <a href="/en/fiche-canadel">Canadel beach</a> is nearby, and <a href="/en/fiche-plage-pramousquier-rayol-canadel">Pramousquier beach</a> is 2 km away via the Voie Verte.</p>
    </div>

